d meditation practice. Different sections of the park will host everything from jazzercise to sword-play. Sunny days will bring out locals lounging on their…"],["Juana Briones Monument","sight",37.8012,-122.4095,"","","","","","r","See the monument erected in honor of this humanitarian and pioneer settler of Yerba Buena (now North Beach)."],["Levi's Plaza Park","sight",37.8024,-122.4014,"1160 Battery St","","","","","r","Located in front of the Levi Strauss headquarters, this immaculately kept little park is perhaps the perfect spot for a picnic... especially if you're exhausted after climbing over Telegraph Hill! It has a soothing fountain as its…"],["Mama's","restaurant",37.8015,-122.4096,"1701 Stockton St","Tue-Sun 8AM-3PM","","","","r","Unbelievably popular place with locals, you only need to see how long the lines are outside at breakfast to understand the popularity of Mama's &mdash; it has become a North Beach institution. In 2007, it won Zagat's \"Best Breakfast in…"],["Fior D'Italia","restaurant",37.8042,-122.4135,"2237 Mason St","11:30AM-10:30PM daily","","","","r","Set a few blocks back from the Wharf area, this is one of the nation's oldest Italian restaurants, and it has been open since 1886. A favorite among locals and visitors alike, it serves authentic Northern Italian cuisine."],["Savoy-Tivoli","bar",37.8002,-122.4073,"1434 Grant Ave","Tue-Fri 5PM-1:30AM, Sat 3PM-1:30AM","","","","r","Roomy, fun open-air bar on Grant Avenue, this bar is a favorite with tourists and locals. It has been around since 1906 and attracts an eclectic yet discerning crowd."],["Bohemian Cigar Store","bar",37.8002,-122.4098,"566 Columbus Ave","Mon-Sat 10AM-midnight, Sun 10AM-11PM","","","","r","Excellent espresso and a relaxed, friendly atmosphere with curbside tables that overlook Washington Square. Its cappuccino is prize-winning."],["Sea lions","sight",37.8106,-122.4116,"Pier 39's West Marina","","","","","r","A short time after the 1989 Loma Prieta earthquake struck, these sea lions moved bag-and-baggage into the west marina at Pier 39. There can be as many as 900 sea lions there during the winter months. In the summertime many of them…"],["Sea Lion Center","sight",37.81062,-122.41099,"Second Level, West Marina, Pier 39","10AM-5PM daily","","","","r","A small free center with limited information and sea lion merchandise. Naturalists from the Aquarium of the Bay are on hand at the center as well as on the dock overlooking the sea lions to answer questions and give presentations about…"],["Street performers","sight",37.8109,-122.4109,"the Crystal Geyser Alpine Spring Water Center Stage","Daily show times: noon, 1:20PM, 2:40PM, 4PM, 5:20PM, 6:30PM, 7:40PM & 8:50PM","","","","r","Colorful jugglers, magicians, clowns, mimes, and comedians of all descriptions entertain Pier 39 visitors throughout the day."],["USS Pampanito Submarine","sight",37.81,-122.41639,"Pier 45","Opens at 9AM daily. Call for closing time","","","","r","This is a National Historic Landmark &mdash; an authentic World War II submarine with many original artifacts on display. Up to 80 personnel ran this submarine and it could be at sea for up to several weeks at a time."],["Amusing America Exhibit","sight",37.8099,-122.417,"Pier 45","10AM-8PM daily","","","","r","An fun exhibit that traces the history of amusement attractions in American cities, with a focus on San Francisco."],["Musee Mecanique","sight",37.8094,-122.4163,"Pier 45, Shed A","Mon-Fri 10AM-7PM, Sat Sun and holidays 10AM-8PM","","","","r","Probably the largest and most extensive antique arcade in the world. Several hundred coin-operated musical instruments, antique arcade games, fortune telling machines, and mechanical dioramas. that date from the turn of the century to…"],["Fishermen's and Seamen's Chapel","sight",37.809,-122.4173,"Pier 45","","","","","r","This tiny chapel is a memorial to the \"Lost Fishermen\"... those that have lost their lives on the seas. Different religions are represented with separate altars on different sides of the tiny chapel. Every year they hold a special…"],["Fish Alley","sight",37.8086,-122.4192,"","","","","","r","Don't forget to go and see the real fishing boats at what's known as Fish Alley &mdash; after all it is \"Fisherman's Wharf\". If you want to see them actually hauling in their catch, you'll have to be there around 6AM to 7AM."],["The Cannery","sight",37.8073,-122.4198,"Del Monte Square","","","","","r","Built in 1907 with its award-winning architecture, the Cannery overlooks San Francisco Bay and once upon a time was the largest peach cannery in the world. Today it's a bustling marketplace featuring three levels of restaurants, shops,…"],["Frequent Flyers","activity",37.8094,-122.4099,"Pier 39","Sun-Thu 11AM-8PM, Fri Sat 10AM-10PM","","","","r","This is an exciting bungee/trampoline combination, suitable for all ages, which allows you to experiment with the dare-devil acrobat inside of you. It's possible to reach heights of up to 20 feet in the air."],["Players Arcade","activity",37.8111,-122.4103,"Pier 39 M-3","Sun 10AM-10PM, Mon-Fri 11:30AM-10PM, Sat 9AM-11PM","","","","r","Have some fun in the largest games arcade in San Francisco."],["Boudin Museum and Bakery Tour","activity",37.8085,-122.4149,"160 Jefferson St","11:30AM-7PM daily","","","","r","Take a tour round the bakery, enjoy some of their interactive exhibits and learn about the history of Boudin."],["The San Francisco Dungeon","activity",37.808,-122.4146,"145 Jefferson St","10AM-9PM daily","","","","r","Somewhat scary theatrical attraction in which the stories of old San Francisco are brought to life with a full theatrical actor cast, special effects, gripping storytelling, 360° sets and an underground boat ride."],["Adventure Cat Sailing Charters","activity",37.8103,-122.4111,"J Dock next to Pier 39","Cruise times vary &mdash; see website","","","","r","Offers a 90-minute bay cruise on a 55-foot luxury catamaran and also sunset cruises in the evening."],["Red & White Fleet","activity",37.8092,-122.4151,"Pier 43½","Cruise times vary &mdash; see website","","","","r","They offer a 1-hour \"Golden Gate Bay Cruise\" which goes under the Golden Gate Bridge and around Alcatraz, a 2 hour \"California Sunset Cruise\" which goes under the Golden Gate Bridge and around Angel Island, and a 90-minute \"Bridge 2…"],["San Francisco Bay Ferry","activity",37.8094,-122.4126,"Pier 41","Times vary &mdash; see website","","","","r","Offering ferry service to/from Alameda/Oakland and Vallejo."],["San Francisco Sailing Company","activity",37.8089,-122.4089,"Pier 39 Dock C","Sail times vary; check website","","","","r","Bay tours under the Golden Gate Bridge and private charters and parties with full catering."],["Alcatraz Cruises","activity",37.8066,-122.4044,"Pier 33, Alcatraz Landing","Cruises start at 8:45AM and continue throughout the day. 10-15 daily departures depending on the time of year. Evening tours offered. Ticket booth at Pier 33 op","","","","r","Information on the island can be found on the National Park Service's website."],["Bistro Boudin","restaurant",37.8086,-122.4146,"160 Jefferson St","Sun-Thu 8AM-9:30PM, Fri Sat 8AM-10PM","","","","r","Home of the sourdough bread with a recipe they've nurtured since 1849, where you can get (among other things) their popular clam chowder in a bread bowl. This is the flagship location of Boudin, where you can shop for gifts here or…"],["Boudin Cafe","restaurant",37.809,-122.4099,"Pier 39","Sun-Thu 8AM-8PM, Fri Sat 8AM-9PM","","","","r","A cafe where you can get Boudin food on Pier 39."],["Chowder and crab sidewalk stands","restaurant",37.8084,-122.4159,"200 Jefferson St","","","","","r","Get clam chowder in a bread bowl, Dungeness crab (in season November through June), fish and chips, shrimp cocktails, calamari salad, etc. from this busy outdoor marketplace. If you're getting a crab, ask for a fresh one and they'll…"],["Cafe Pescatore","restaurant",37.8063,-122.414,"2455 Mason St","Mon-Thu 7AM-10:30AM, 11:30AM-10PM, Fri-Sun 7AM-10PM","","","","r","A mid-range Italian trattoria that focuses on the staples of Italian food like pasta, pizza, and risottos. It being Fisherman's Wharf, they do have a particular focus on seafood however."],["Joanie's Happy Days Diner","restaurant",37.8064,-122.4193,"1329 Columbus Ave","7AM-5PM","","","","r","Good and fresh breakfast and lunch service at a reasonable price. Fast service and big variation result in a full diner every morning."],["Pompei's Grotto","restaurant",37.8081,-122.4181,"340 Jefferson St","11AM-?? daily","","","","r","Much quieter, less expensive, and less touristy than the big name Fisherman's Wharf restaurants; excellent food, with an emphasis on seafood and Italian specialties, served by nice people. Still owned and managed by the Pompei family,…"],["Castagnola's","restaurant",37.8082,-122.4175,"286 Jefferson St","11AM-9PM daily","","","","r","Voted San Francisco's No. 1 Seafood and Family Restaurant of 1998 by the National Academy of Restaurant Evaluation and The Best of San Francisco Pocket Guide. They specialize in seafood and Italian cuisine, complimented by quality…"],["Nicks Lighthouse","restaurant",37.8085,-122.4161,"2815 Taylor St","Sun-Thu 11AM-10:30PM, Fri Sat 11AM-11PM","","","","r","Warm and aromatic Italian restaurant serving popular family fare."],["Sabella and LaTorre","restaurant",37.8084,-122.416,"2809 Taylor St","Restaurant: Sun-Thu 10AM-10:45PM, Fri Sat 10AM-12:45AM; crab stand: 7AM-10:45PM","","","","r","A family owned restaurant that's been open since 1927 providing fresh seafood, family fare, and a full bar. They're known in particular for their \"cracked crab\"."],["Scoma's Restaurant","restaurant",37.8089,-122.4181,"Pier 47 on Al Scoma Way","Mon-Thu 11:30AM-10PM, Fri-Sun 11:30AM-10:30PM; closed Thanksgiving Day, Christmas Eve, and Christmas Day. The Bar is open daily 30 minutes prior to lunch servic","","","","r","Overlooking the bay and Alcatraz, and nestled among the fishing boats on Pier 47, this restaurant is popular among locals and tourists alike for its fresh seafood."],["Las Margaritas","bar",37.8071,-122.4195,"Del Monte Square, 2nd Level, South Bldg","10AM-11:30PM daily","","","","r","A Fruit Margarita in the Cannery anyone?"],["Filbert Street","sight",37.8002,-122.4184,"","","","","","r","At a 31.5% grade, this is one of the very steepest streets in the entire Western Hemisphere. Like many of the steeper streets in the city, it has steps along the sidewalk and its own special set of parking rules, so that people and cars…"],["Francisco Street","sight",37.804,-122.4191,"","","","","","r","This block contains twelve spectacular mansions in a variety of styles. It is very close to the crooked section of Lombard Street and is worth the minor detour on the way."],["Bimbo's 365 Club","bar",37.8037,-122.4156,"1025 Columbus Ave","Box office: Mon-Fri 10AM-4PM, Club hours: Vary","","","","r","Bimbo's is a glamorous upscale event venue and nightclub that holds up to 700 people. It has three bars, a dance floor and stage. Robin Williams did his act here quite regularly."],["La Trappe Cafe","bar",37.802,-122.413,"800 Greenwich St","6PM-midnight daily","","","","r","A great beer bar and restaurtant hidden in the lower part of North Beach. Out of the way of most tourists because of its low profile. Huge Belgian Beer selection, and other craft brews from around the world. Restaurant offers mussels…"]]}